# Project Context — Bukovel App Design System

## What we are building

A React Native mobile app for **Bukovel** — the largest ski resort in Ukraine.
Stack: Expo (SDK 52+), React Native, TypeScript, Reanimated 3.
Platforms: iOS and Android only. Web is a separate project — ignore it.

The app covers: ski pass booking, hotel booking, transfer booking, resort services, trip planning, events, interactive resort map, and user profile (BukovelID).

## Who is working on this

**Simon** — Design Director at The Gradient (Lviv). Responsible for:
- Figma design system
- React Native design system (this project)
- Figma screens and user flows

Simon works as a **vibecoder** — he drives architecture and design decisions, uses Cursor + Figma MCP to build components, and is not a full-time developer. Keep explanations plain. Never over-explain obvious things.

The dev team (Gradient + Bukovel side) will consume the components built here.

## Development context

- **Quick testing**: Expo Go app on physical device, scan QR from terminal. This is the primary method.
- **The app's main entry during development** is the Design System preview screen — not a real app screen.
- Figma MCP is connected in Cursor and is the source of truth for design tokens and component specs.
- Primitives (raw colors) and semantic tokens are provided directly from Figma — never invent or guess color values.
- Font: **Bukovel** (custom brand font). Font files will be provided. Never substitute another font.

## Design system structure

### Colors — 2 layers
1. **Primitives** (`src/theme/primitives.ts`) — raw hex values, numeric scale (Brand100–Brand900, Neutral100–900, etc.). Never used directly in components.
2. **Semantic tokens** (`src/theme/tokens.ts`) — colors by role: `bgWinter`, `intPrimary`, `textOnCard`, `iconOnInt`, etc. These are the only colors components reference.

Two themes: `winter` (default) and `summer`. Both must always be in sync.

### Typography
Variant names match Figma token names in camelCase: `body1Highlight`, `ctaLarge`, `captionLabel`, etc.
All text in the app goes through the `AppTypography` atom — never raw `<Text>`.
`allowFontScaling={false}` always.

### Spacing
Base unit: 4px. Named scale: `tiny` (4), `small` (8), `medium` (12), `large` (16), `extraLarge` (20), `xxLarge` (24), `xxxLarge` (32).
Never use raw numbers for spacing in components.

### Border Radius
Figma uses `radius(N)` tokens where the pixel value = N × 4. Named scale in `@theme/radius.ts`:
`small` (4), `medium` (8), `large` (12), `extraLarge` (16), `xxLarge` (24), `full` (9999).
Never hardcode radius numbers in components. Always use `radius.*`.
When pulling from Figma, always check that every object has a named radius token applied — if not, flag it and ask Simon to update Figma first.

### Icons
Two sources:
- **Iconoir React Native** for standard UI icons. kebab-case name → PascalCase component: `arrow-right` → `ArrowRight`.
- **Custom SVG** for resort-specific icons (gondola, ski lift, slopes, etc.) in `src/assets/icons/custom/`.
All icons go through the `AppIcon` atom. Never import icon libraries directly in feature components.

### Component structure (atomic design)
Every component lives in its own folder with exactly these files:
- `ComponentName.tsx` — JSX and rendering logic only
- `ComponentName.types.ts` — all TypeScript types and prop definitions
- `ComponentName.styles.ts` — all StyleSheet.create() calls, receives tokens as argument
- `index.ts` — single re-export line
- `README.md` — states table, variants, Figma link, usage example

Atomic categories:
- `atoms/` — single-purpose: AppButton, AppInput, AppTypography, AppIcon, AppBadge, AppTag, AppToggle, AppCheckbox
- `molecules/` — composed of atoms: AppFormField, AppListItem, AppSearchBar, AppCardHeader
- `organisms/` — complex, full sections: AppModal, AppBottomSheet, AppForm, AppDatePicker

Component prefix: always `App` — `AppButton` not `Button`, `AppInput` not `Input`.

### Design System preview screen
Lives at `src/screens/DesignSystem/`. This is the app entry during development.
Shows all components with all states. Searchable. Filterable by category and Figma page.
Registry file `registry.ts` is auto-maintained — updated every time a component is created or gets a new state.
Every text state must include long-text and 2-line wrap test entries.

## What each rule file does

| File | Scope | Purpose |
|------|-------|---------|
| `00-conventions.mdc` | always | Naming, file structure, imports, prop naming patterns |
| `01-design-tokens.mdc` | `src/**` | Token system rules, what components can and cannot reference |
| `02-component-from-figma.mdc` | `src/components/**` | How to structure components, state detection, registry update |
| `03-icons.mdc` | `src/**` | Iconoir naming, custom icon detection, AppIcon usage |
| `04-design-system-preview.mdc` | `src/screens/DesignSystem/**` | registry.ts rules, DS screen structure, text stress tests |
| `05-quality-checks.mdc` | `src/components/**` | Token misuse, missing states, prop consistency, README requirement |
| `06-figma-mcp-workflow.mdc` | on demand | Figma MCP inspection, token mapping, off-grid flagging |

## What the skill file does

`SKILL-rn-component-from-figma.md` — fires when a Figma link is pasted.
10-step workflow: inspect via MCP → confirm plan with user → build files → map tokens → resolve icons → handle missing states → add text stress tests → write README → update registry → output summary.

**Always confirm the plan before writing any code.**

## Key rules to never break

- No hardcoded hex colors anywhere in component files
- No hardcoded spacing numbers anywhere in component files
- No hardcoded border radius numbers anywhere in component files — always `radius.*`
- No raw `<Text>` — always `<AppTypography>`
- No direct Iconoir or SVG imports in feature components — always `<AppIcon>`
- Both themes (winter + summer) must always be updated together
- `registry.ts` must be updated every time a component is created or changed
- Always ask about missing states before finishing a component
- Always add long-text and wrap-test entries for every text state
- When pulling from Figma, always flag objects with no corner radius applied — never guess
